{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1516138456,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM1ODExNDE0OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2082#issuecomment-358114148"},"message":"I wonder, if given this idea we could/should absorb (virtually) all changes in master which do not touch datalad/metadata into 0.9.x?\n\nOn one hand I am not entirely enthusiastic about modularizing it away or moving into yet another collection of plugins -- we do need search functionality and IMHO it should be visible at the top level API.  BUT indeed with some work implementation could be made \"Datalad agnostic\" and support other ways to collate multiple datasets, etc and then useful/usable for other projects.  But I think it will not really address any problem and thus shouldn't get time investment ATM (my 1c).","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1516182065,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM1ODI0OTg4Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2082#issuecomment-358249883"},"message":"One comment: I think it is critical to distinguish two very different aspects of metadata handling that seem to be conflated in some of our discussions -- but really should not be.\n\n- **metadata aggregation and representation in a dataset**. This has to be done right, and I doubt that anybody would want to support multiple simultaneous representations. The state in 0.9 is basically only \"working\" because we limit the amount of metadata to a handful of keys. Action is needed here, if any progress is desired.\n\n- **applications that use aggregated metadata**. Everything is optional here. There could be a search implementation like there is in 0.9 that sits on top of the aggregated metadata, extracts the 5 keys that it cares about, and prints the path to the dataset. There can be a whoosh-based SQL-like search in addition, without having ANY impact on the actual dataset handling. There can also be other search implementations (graph-based, ...) inside or outside datalad that are compatible with our aggregated metadata as an input source. If somebody would want to build an external DB and fill it with our metadata for whatever queries, all they would care about it the representation of the aggregated metadata, and how to extract it from a datalad dataset, nothing else.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1516187147,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM1ODI3MTY0MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2082#issuecomment-358271641"},"message":"That distinction is a good point.\nHowever, that doesn't suggest a clear line what to include in the core. Metadata representation is a concept, not any code. Parsers, the `metadata` command and aggregation are producing those representations, so that would suggest to include those pieces in the core. On the other hand, it's more about a defined parser interface not actual parsers themselves. And aggregation isn't necessarily needed. So, I'm not sure yet, where to draw the line.\n\nBut generally I agree to this:\n\n\u003e Heck, this could be a set of plugins...and it would be a good reason to elevate the plugin interface to behave like full-scale commands.... I start to like this... Maybe this could be a general path for additions/changes of datalad components. Implement them as plugins, bring them to people, let people decide what works and which way and only eventually move proven pieces into the core code base.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1518254798,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NDYzODU1Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2082#issuecomment-364638557"},"message":"With #2115 we now have two different search modes/styles that are implemented completely separate from the metadata aggregation tools. I consider the aggregation aspect a core piece, while search is an application.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1518254799,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTQ2NzkzMDc4MA=="},"status":2}]}